       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Your patient has normal kidney and liver function and no allergies, so nothing in their profile explains a dose that high. Doses above 200 mg raise the risk of serotonin toxicity, QT effects, GI effects, and agitation, and they haven't been shown to work better.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n\n- **A dose of 200 mg PO once daily**, which is the maximum labeled dose. Typical titration starts at 25\u201350 mg and increases in 25\u201350 mg steps at intervals of a week or more.\n- **A different dose**, if 400 mg was a typo. For example, 40 mg or 100 mg.\n- **400 mg on purpose**, for example in a specialist-directed, treatment-resistant case. If so, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording the intentional above-maximum dose and your rationale. Please also confirm that you've reviewed interacting drugs and the patient's baseline ECG.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
